.SH Default keybinds
Two mirrored clusters bind the same letters: \f[CR]<space>m\&...\f[R]
and \f[CR]\[aq]\&...\f[R].
The \f[CR]\[aq]\f[R] cluster always works; the \f[CR]<space>m\f[R]
cluster is shadowed by the tasks plugin inside markdown buffers
(filetype\-scoped bindings win).
Bare \f[CR]\[aq]\f[R] is deliberately unbound \[em] an exact match fires
immediately, which would make the two\-key \f[CR]\[aq]x\f[R] sequences
unreachable; toggle is the double\-tap \f[CR]\[aq]\[aq]\f[R] instead.
.PP
